        "original_id": "7945fb9c-f563-5162-a537-467abc1ee1bd",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Billy J. Kramer, Mike Maxfield, William Howard Ashton\n- Organizations: The Dakotas\n- Roles: lead vocalist, songwriter, guitarist, pop singer\n- Places: Liverpool, Manchester, England\n\nFacts:\n- Billy J. Kramer was born as William Howard Ashton on 19 August 1943 and is an English pop singer.\n- Mike Maxfield was born on 23 February 1944 in Manchester, England, and is an English songwriter and guitarist.\n- Mike Maxfield became known as a member of The Dakotas.\n- During the 1960s, Billy J. Kramer, a Liverpudlian singer, was the lead vocalist for The Dakotas.\n- The Dakotas are most closely associated with Billy J. Kramer.",
